{"skill":{"slug":"language-learning","displayName":"Language Learning Tutor"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769733977182,"changelog":"Initial release: AI language tutor supporting 100+ languages with 7 teaching modes (vocab builder, grammar lessons, conversation practice, flashcard drills, script/writing systems, cultural context, exam prep)","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":10735,"sha256":"bb9b988f3423308577acf60cbd22b7e734f64ba6960b96f0b36fce426f160fed","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2244,"sha256":"2fabc61eb1e068859515bba2638ec2a73c51ef7b7c4bf1bc6a5c92f61c9a602f","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789023864651,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"8e14facdef45a5a5b18585fcc7ae162340e76fe02f30695280f57ee3e3b03a9a","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/8e14facdef45a5a5b18585fcc7ae162340e76fe02f30695280f57ee3e3b03a9a","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: language-learning\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is benign. The `_meta.json` file contains standard metadata. The `SKILL.md` file provides comprehensive instructions for an AI language tutor, detailing teaching modes, session structures, and adaptive learning strategies. All instructions are clearly aligned with the stated purpose of language learning and lack any indicators of malicious intent, such as data exfiltration, unauthorized execution, persistence mechanisms, or adversarial prompt injection attempts against the agent.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160345719},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":17,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789023864651},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a markdown-only language tutor skill with broad routing language but no hidden code, persistence, credential access, or external actions.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill does not request local filesystem, network, shell, browser, credential, account, or mutation access; its instructions are proportional to an educational assistant.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The inspected package contains a single non-executable SKILL.md artifact and no install scripts, dependencies, remote fetches, or bundled code.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The trigger description and quick-command examples are broad enough that the skill may activate for generic translation, grammar, travel, or writing prompts, but the behavior remains aligned with language tutoring.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill suggests tracking learner progress within sessions, but it does not define persistent storage, background workers, privilege changes, or cross-session hooks.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is language learning, and the artifact's capabilities are tutoring modes such as vocabulary, grammar, conversation practice, flashcards, scripts, culture, and exam prep.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Installers should expect this skill to steer many language, translation, grammar, and travel-phrase requests into a tutoring workflow. That broadness may be inconvenient in ambiguous conversations, but the inspected artifact does not show code execution, credential handling, data exfiltration, destructive behavior, or hidden persistence.","findings":"[SQP-1] expected: The broad description and keyword-rich activation language are real routing-quality concerns, but they do not introduce high-impact authority or hidden behavior.\n[SQP-1] expected: The quick-command examples are generic and may over-trigger, but they are examples of language-learning activities rather than unrelated actions.\n[EA3] expected: Supporting many human languages is broad, but it is coherent with the advertised purpose of an all-language tutor and is not evidence of unsafe scope creep.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789023864651}}}}}